There are already projects such as [SeerahBook](https://seerahbook.com/?utm_source=chatgpt.com), [Seerah.page](https://seerah.page/?utm_source=chatgpt.com) and [Seerah Academy](https://seerah.academy/?utm_source=chatgpt.com). Your project could differentiate itself by combining comprehensive historical coverage, rigorous source verification, an encyclopedia of miracles and prophecies, and an immersive user experience.

**I would start with the knowledge database before building the frontend.** The hardest and most valuable part of this project is not the programming but collecting, organizing and verifying the information.

The outline above is a proposed architecture, not yet a complete verified historical database. No source can document literally every moment of his life, but the project could aim to cover every reasonably documented event, narration and aspect of his Seerah.

The ultimate vision would be a digital museum, historical encyclopedia and Islamic learning platform dedicated entirely to the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.